Write the research block exactly as Phase A specifies: a `### <SOURCE_ID>` heading  with source_id, subcategory, source_name, official_url, verified_at, verification_result, source_pages, key_regions, key_interactions, complexity, stack_clues and limitations. Map only URLs that returned 2xx above. A page that failed goes in limitations with its status. Every interaction is marked observed only if the fetched markup supports it, otherwise inferred.

Then, after the block, emit one fenced JSON object with the proposed inventory row:

```json
{"rows": [{"source_id": "NEWS-09", "subcategory": "...", "source_name": "...", "source_url": "https://...", "verified_at": "YYYY-MM-DD", "verification_method": "...", "verification_result": "verified", "evidence_reference": "", "source_pages": [{"url": "https://...", "title": "...", "local_file": "index.html"}], "key_regions": ["..."], "key_interactions": [{"name": "...", "evidence": "observed", "notes": "..."}], "complexity": "medium", "stack_clues": "...", "limitations": "..."}]}
```

Exactly one row. Leave evidence_reference as an empty string — I fill it with the evidence file path. Do not include model_id, approved_at, approved_by or approval_reference: the model is recorded by me, and approval is the project lead's decision, not ours.
